(docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #111, owner ruling 2026-08-29, GitHub #34, Option 1:
 a collection placed inside another collection is a copy, not a shared
 reference. `outer`'s literal slot copies `inner`'s block at construction
 time, so mutating `inner` afterward never reaches `outer`. Master-probed
 on 0.4.14 before this fix: `outer` showed `[[777, 2], 3]` - the
 pointer-in behaviour this closes.)

a list called inner is [1, 2].
a list called outer is [inner, 3].
Set element 1 of inner to 777.
print outer.
print inner.
